### Food Delivery Platform - User Service
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (named requests pass ids between calls).
### Run the requests from top to bottom: 1 -> 2 -> 3 ...
###
### Login returns an access token (JWT). Every other call sends it (Authorization: Bearer), and only the token says
### who the caller is (the admin APIs require the role PLATFORM_ADMIN).

# Direct to the service:
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
# Or through the API Gateway (same paths):
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

# Bootstrap admin from your .env file (BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL / BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD)
@adminEmail = admin@fooddelivery.local
@adminPassword = ChangeMe123

# Change this before step 1 if the customer already exists (409 Conflict)
@customerEmail = priya.sharma@example.com
@customerPassword = Priya1234

@customerId = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
# Every call carries the access token of a sign-in above (valid 15 minutes: sign in again after that).
@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@adminId = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.userId}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@addressId = {{addAddress.response.body.$.id}}


### ============================ AUTH ============================

### 1. Register a customer (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}",
  "fullName": "Priya Sharma",
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

### 2. Log in as the customer (200) -> customerId, accessToken, and the cookie fd_refresh_customer
###    "role" is optional: with it, another kind of account gets 403 WRONG_ACCOUNT_TYPE
# @name customerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}",
  "role": "CUSTOMER"
}

### 2a. New access token from the refresh cookie (REST Client keeps cookies between requests) -> 200 and a new cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "CUSTOMER" }

### 2b. The public key services use to check access tokens (user-service only; not routed by the gateway)
GET http://localhost:8081/.well-known/jwks.json

### 2c. Sign out of the customer area (204, cookie removed); a refresh afterwards answers 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "CUSTOMER" }

### 3. Register a restaurant owner (role chosen at sign-up)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner.spicehub@example.com",
  "password": "Owner1234",
  "fullName": "Arjun Mehta",
  "role": "RESTAURANT_ADMIN"
}

### 4. Validation error example (400 with field errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short",
  "fullName": ""
}

### 5. Wrong password (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "WrongPass1"
}


### ========================= MY PROFILE =========================

### 6. Get my profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 7. Update my profile
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Priya S. Sharma",
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

### 8. Change my password (204)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{customerPassword}}",
  "newPassword": "{{customerPassword}}x"
}

### 9. Change it back (so step 2 keeps working)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{customerPassword}}x",
  "newPassword": "{{customerPassword}}"
}


### ========================= MY ADDRESSES =========================

### 10. Add an address (the first one becomes the default) -> addressId
# @name addAddress
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "HOME",
  "line1": "12 MG Road",
  "line2": "Near Metro Station",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "postalCode": "560001",
  "country": "India",
  "latitude": 12.975400,
  "longitude": 77.606800
}

### 11. Add a work address and make it the default
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "WORK",
  "line1": "Tech Park, Tower B",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "postalCode": "560103",
  "country": "India",
  "makeDefault": true
}

### 12. List my addresses (default first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 13. Update the home address
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses/{{addressId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "HOME",
  "line1": "14 MG Road",
  "city": "Bengaluru",
  "state": "Karnataka",
  "postalCode": "560001",
  "country": "India"
}

### 14. Make the home address the default again
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/me/addresses/{{addressId}}/default
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ========================= ADMIN: USERS =========================

### 15. Log in as the platform admin -> adminId
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

### 16. List users (paged, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users?page=0&size=20&sort=createdAt,desc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 17. Search + filter: active customers matching "priya"
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users?search=priya&role=CUSTOMER&status=ACTIVE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 18. User details (created date, last login, address count)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 19. Deactivate the customer (reason is required)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{customerId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Request-Id: demo-deactivate-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Multiple chargebacks reported"
}

### 20. The deactivated customer cannot log in now (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### 21. Activate the customer again
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{customerId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Chargebacks resolved with the bank"
}

### 22. Change the customer's role
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{customerId}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "DELIVERY_PARTNER",
  "reason": "Customer joined as a delivery partner"
}

### 23. Audit history of the customer (newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{customerId}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 24. A customer calling an admin API (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### 25. Admin trying to deactivate themselves (422)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/users/{{adminId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Testing the safety rule"
}


### ======================= EVENTS (Kafka, Phases 7-8) =======================
### Every successful registration writes UserRegistered (topic fooddelivery.user.registered, key = userId)
### to the transactional outbox, in the same transaction as the new user; the outbox relay publishes it.
### Kafka down? Registration still works; the event waits in outbox_events and is sent when Kafka is back.
### Messages: Kafka UI http://localhost:8090

### UserRegistered schema in Schema Registry
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects/fooddelivery.user.registered-value/versions/latest

### All registered schemas
GET http://localhost:8091/subjects

### ========================= OPERATIONS =========================

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### OpenAPI document (Swagger UI: http://localhost:8081/swagger-ui.html)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v3/api-docs
